          "However, free versions impose deliberate restrictions. Most tools watermark every exported video, forcing you to either display their logo or pay for a subscription. Output resolution is often capped at 720p or 1080p (rarely 4K), and there are monthly video export limits—typically 10–15 minutes of finished footage across all projects. AI features like advanced script rewriting, predictive scene selection, or object‐aware editing are either disabled or severely limited. For instance, InVideo’s free plan caps the number of AI “templates” you can customize per month, while Pictory’s summarization tool truncates long articles into a maximum of 15 minutes of video per month. You cannot remove the watermark, but you can work around it by placing your own channel logo in the corner or using a photo overlay—although it’s not a permanent solution if you aim for a professional appearance.",
          "In practice, the free tier is enough for three key scenarios: (1) you are building a YouTube channel from scratch and need to test multiple video styles without financial risk; (2) you produce short, low‑stakes content like quick tutorials, “shorts”, or channel trailers where a watermark is acceptable; (3) you are a student or hobbyist sharing educational videos for a small audience. For those use cases, the free versions are surprisingly robust—many users can maintain a steady upload schedule of 3–4 videos per month without hitting the export limits. As your channel grows and you need 4K resolution, custom branding, or advanced AI editing, it makes sense to upgrade, but the free tier has let you prove your concept at zero cost."
