      "In 2026, the landscape of AI 3D modeling has matured significantly. The quality of free-tier outputs rivals what paid plugins offered just two years ago. Use cases range from rapid prototyping of furniture for interior design to generating low-poly characters for mobile games. Product designers use these tools to visualize concepts before manufacturing, while educators create interactive 3D models for STEM lessons. The ability to iterate quickly—generating dozens of variations in a single session—makes AI 3D generators indispensable for anyone who needs to validate ideas without committing to a full production pipeline. However, free accounts come with trade-offs that are important to understand before diving in.",
      "Among the most generous free offerings, <a href=\"https://www.meshy.ai\" class=\"text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-700 underline font-medium\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Meshy</a> stands out with its text-to-3D and image-to-3D capabilities, providing 100 free credits per month—enough to generate around 10 to 15 detailed models. The free tier includes a visible watermark and limits export resolution to 256x256 texture maps. <a href=\"https://spline.design\" class=\"text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-700 underline font-medium\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Spline</a> offers a browser-based 3D editor with AI-assisted generation, perfect for interactive web graphics; its free plan allows up to 3 public projects and exports with a Spline branding. For realistic object scanning, <a href=\"https://lumalabs.ai\" class=\"text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-700 underline font-medium\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Luma AI</a> provides a free tier that lets you capture real-world objects via your smartphone camera and convert them into 3D models, but output meshes are watermarked and limited to 10 captures per month. These platforms are excellent starting points for anyone exploring 3D creation without financial commitment."
