          "<strong class=\"text-slate-800\">Image-to-3D Conversion:</strong> Upload a single photo or a multi-angle set to reconstruct a 3D model. Free plans usually restrict the image resolution (max 1024px) and number of angles (1–3 images). This feature excels for digitizing real-world objects like sculptures, toys, or architectural details, though the resulting mesh may need cleanup in an external editor.",
          "<strong class=\"text-slate-800\">Real-time Mesh Editing:</strong> Many free tools include a basic 3D viewer where you can adjust scale, rotation, and material colors. Advanced editing like vertex painting or topology optimization is reserved for paid tiers. This is sufficient for quick previews but not for production-ready modifications.",
          "<strong class=\"text-slate-800\">Export Format Support:</strong> Free accounts typically export only .glb or .obj files, sometimes with reduced texture quality. Missing formats like .fbx (for animation), .usdz (for AR), or .stl (for 3D printing) force users to convert files through third-party tools, which can degrade quality.",
